# Continuous orchestration

Recover the active dirty PRD slice before selecting new work. For each slice: plan, freeze contracts, implement, run focused/full gates, synchronize canonical docs plus one trace block, obtain required independent reviews, correct findings, verify the immutable commit, then continue the next dependency-ready local slice.

Use one integration master. Before multi-agent work, read `.cursor/rules/50-multi-agent-orchestration.mdc`; use at most three disjoint writers and only non-duplicative reviewers/researchers. Missing Docker, browser, service, Linux, staging, or production evidence blocks only the corresponding claim and remains explicit.

Stop only for an undecided product/architecture choice, repeated unsafe failure, missing authority/secret, destructive/external/production work, completed roadmap, or session limit. Leave Git/traceability as the recoverable checkpoint. Local commits are allowed by the active start/resume workflow; never push or mutate production/DNS/Cloudflare.
